WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.564
Read a GPU instance specification as a complete system.

00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:09.563
Start with the exact accelerator model, count, architecture, and VRAM.

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:14.996
VRAM constrains model weights, context cache, batch size, and training state.

00:00:14.996 --> 00:00:21.733
Two instances advertised as one GPU can deliver very different performance and software compatibility.

00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:29.340
Confirm whether the device is dedicated, partitioned, or shared and whether the intended framework supports it.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:36.511
Virtual CPU and system RAM support tokenization, data loading, decompression, preprocessing, and the serving application.

00:00:36.511 --> 00:00:41.510
Too few CPU cores can leave an expensive GPU waiting.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:46.943
Insufficient RAM can prevent model loading or force slow disk use.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:51.507
Examine local ephemeral storage and attached persistent-disk options separately.

00:00:51.507 --> 00:00:59.983
Ephemeral disks may be fast but disappear with the instance, while persistent disks survive and continue generating charges.

00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:05.851
Network specifications influence dataset movement, model downloads, distributed work, and service response.

00:01:05.851 --> 00:01:11.284
Published maximum bandwidth may depend on instance size or traffic conditions.

00:01:11.284 --> 00:01:21.064
Region and availability zone affect latency to users and other services, data-residency obligations, and whether a desired GPU can be provisioned.

00:01:21.064 --> 00:01:27.367
Place related compute and storage deliberately to avoid unnecessary transfer or cross-zone charges.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:31.496
Hourly price is only the visible starting point.

00:01:31.496 --> 00:01:38.233
Check minimum billing increments, operating-system charges, discounts, interruption terms, and storage and network rates.

00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:44.536
Before building automation around an instance type, verify account quotas and actual capacity.

00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:53.446
A catalog listing does not guarantee that the GPU is available in the required region at the required time.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:58.445
Maintain at least one acceptable alternative configuration for important work.
